I have enough signal. Here are the gaps I found that are **from the refactor itself** (not in TD files, not the Resend integration).




## Infra-pipeline holes

12. **`platform-shopify-admin` is not built or deployed by CI.** `platform-front` has the full Vite-build + `gcloud storage rsync` step. `platform-shopify-admin` — the iframe Shopify Admin actually loads when a merchant opens the app — has no CI job, no bucket, no deploy YAML, not even an `API_URL` injection. The iframe-contract fix (`0897350`) is code-complete but unshippable today.
13. **Stale package reference in frontend types** — `platform-front/src/types/dashboard.ts:1` says `// Mirrors the subset of @new-one-two/types needed by the dashboard.` The old monorepo `@new-one-two/*` package namespace was renamed to `@platform-back/*`. Just a comment, but it's the tell that sections of `dashboard.ts` haven't been re-audited against the new types.

## Carry-over scale issues the refactor made worse

14. **Deploy job state lives in a per-process `Map` in `orchestrator.ts`.** Old deploy was sync-in-request so it didn't matter; new deploy returns a `jobId` and the dashboard subscribes via SSE. With `maxScale: 10` on the API Cloud Run service and no sticky routing, the merchant's SSE connection will hit a different instance from the one running the deploy and see nothing. TD-001 tracks the UI wiring but not this state problem.
15. **Pub/Sub progress fan-out has the same per-process subscription problem** (`pubsub/progress-subscriber.ts`). Present in the old design too, but in the refactor there are now *two* long-lived SSE streams (generation + deploy) running on a service configured to autoscale.

